@startuml Weaver in CI/CD Pipeline

!define GITHUB_COLOR #24292E
!define BUILD_COLOR #3498DB
!define TEST_COLOR #9B59B6
!define WEAVER_COLOR #E74C3C
!define DEPLOY_COLOR #2ECC71

title CI/CD Pipeline with Weaver Validation Gate

actor "Developer" as Dev
participant "GitHub\nActions" as GHA #GITHUB_COLOR
participant "Build\nStage" as Build #BUILD_COLOR
participant "Test\nStage" as Test #TEST_COLOR
participant "Weaver\nlive-check" as Weaver #WEAVER_COLOR
participant "Validation\nGate" as Gate
participant "Deploy\nStage" as Deploy #DEPLOY_COLOR
database "Production" as Prod

== Pull Request Created ==

Dev -> GHA : git push / create PR
activate GHA

GHA -> Build : cargo build --release --features otel
activate Build

Build -> Build : Compile all crates
Build -> Build : Run clippy
Build -> Build : Run fmt check

alt Build fails
    Build --> GHA : ❌ Build failed
    GHA --> Dev : ❌ Cannot proceed
    deactivate Build
    deactivate GHA
else Build succeeds
    Build --> GHA : ✅ Build passed
    deactivate Build

    == Test Execution Phase ==

    GHA -> Test : cargo test --features otel
    activate Test

    par Run tests in parallel
        Test -> Test : Unit tests
        and
        Test -> Test : Integration tests
        and
        Test -> Test : Docker tests
    end

    alt Tests fail
        Test --> GHA : ❌ Tests failed
        GHA --> Dev : ❌ Cannot proceed
        deactivate Test
        deactivate GHA
    else Tests pass
        Test --> GHA : ✅ Tests passed
        note right
            **Traditional CI stops here**
            Ships to prod with potential
            false positives!
        end note

        == Weaver Validation Phase ==

        GHA -> Weaver : Start live-check
        activate Weaver

        note right of Weaver #WEAVER_COLOR
            ```yaml
            # .github/workflows/ci.yml
            - name: Start Weaver validation
              run: |
                weaver registry live-check \
                  --registry registry/ \
                  --otlp-grpc-port 4317 \
                  --format json \
                  --output ./validation_output &
                WEAVER_PID=$!
                echo $WEAVER_PID > weaver.pid
                sleep 3
            ```
        end note

        Weaver -> Weaver : Load registry
        Weaver -> Weaver : Start OTLP listener :4317

        GHA -> Test : cargo test --features otel
        note right
            ```yaml
            - name: Run tests with OTLP export
              env:
                OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT: http://localhost:4317
              run: |
                cargo test --features otel
            ```

            Tests export telemetry to Weaver!
        end note

        Test -> Weaver : Stream OTLP telemetry
        loop For each test
            Weaver -> Weaver : Validate against schema
            Weaver -> Weaver : Accumulate statistics
        end

        Test --> GHA : Tests complete

        deactivate Test

        GHA -> Weaver : Stop and generate report
        note right
            ```yaml
            - name: Stop Weaver and get report
              run: |
                WEAVER_PID=$(cat weaver.pid)
                kill -HUP $WEAVER_PID
                wait $WEAVER_PID
                WEAVER_EXIT=$?
            ```
        end note

        Weaver -> Weaver : Generate statistics
        Weaver -> Weaver : Write live_check.json

        Weaver --> GHA : exit_code + report
        deactivate Weaver

        == Validation Gate ==

        GHA -> Gate : Check validation results
        activate Gate

        Gate -> Gate : Read live_check.json
        note right
            ```yaml
            - name: Parse validation report
              run: |
                VIOLATIONS=$(jq '.statistics.advice_level_counts.violation // 0' \
                             validation_output/live_check.json)

                if [ "$VIOLATIONS" -gt 0 ]; then
                  echo "❌ Weaver validation FAILED"
                  exit 1
                fi
            ```
        end note

        Gate -> Gate : Count violations
        Gate -> Gate : Check coverage

        alt Violations found
            Gate --> GHA : ❌ VALIDATION FAILED
            note right #E74C3C
                **Validation Report:**
                ```json
                {
                  "statistics": {
                    "advice_level_counts": {
                      "violation": 5
                    },
                    "registry_coverage": 0.23
                  }
                }
                ```

                **Examples of violations:**
                - Required attribute 'container.id' missing
                - Type mismatch on 'exit_code'
                - Missing required attribute 'test.isolated'

                **These prove false positives!**
            end note

            GHA -> GHA : Fail workflow
            GHA -> GHA : Block PR merge
            GHA --> Dev : ❌ Cannot merge - Fix violations
            note left of Dev
                Developer sees:
                - Which tests have false positives
                - Which attributes are missing
                - Exact violation details

                Must fix before merge allowed.
            end note

            deactivate Gate
            deactivate GHA

        else No violations
            Gate --> GHA : ✅ VALIDATION PASSED
            note right #2ECC71
                **Validation Report:**
                ```json
                {
                  "statistics": {
                    "advice_level_counts": {
                      "violation": 0,
                      "improvement": 2,
                      "information": 5
                    },
                    "registry_coverage": 0.85,
                    "total_entities": 150
                  }
                }
                ```

                **All checks passed:**
                ✓ All required attributes present
                ✓ Types match schema
                ✓ Hermetic isolation proven
                ✓ 85% registry coverage

                **Features proven to work!**
            end note

            deactivate Gate

            == Merge and Deploy ==

            GHA -> GHA : Enable merge button
            GHA --> Dev : ✅ PR can be merged
            Dev -> GHA : Merge PR

            GHA -> Deploy : Trigger deployment
            activate Deploy

            Deploy -> Deploy : Build release artifacts
            Deploy -> Deploy : Tag version
            Deploy -> Prod : Deploy to production
            note right #2ECC71
                **SAFE TO DEPLOY**

                Every feature has been validated:
                - Tests passed
                - Weaver validated
                - No false positives
                - Runtime behavior proven

                Can deploy with confidence!
            end note

            Deploy --> GHA : ✅ Deployed
            deactivate Deploy
            GHA --> Dev : ✅ Deployed to production
            deactivate GHA
        end
    end
end

== The Protection This Provides ==

note over Dev, Prod #FFE5E5
    **WITHOUT Weaver Gate:**

    1. Developer writes fake implementation
    2. Tests pass (false positive)
    3. PR merged
    4. Deployed to production
    5. Breaks in production
    6. Customers affected

    **Time to discover: Days/Weeks**
    **Impact: Production incidents**
end note

note over Dev, Prod #E5FFE5
    **WITH Weaver Gate:**

    1. Developer writes fake implementation
    2. Tests pass (still passes)
    3. Weaver detects missing telemetry
    4. Violations reported
    5. PR blocked
    6. Developer fixes before merge

    **Time to discover: Minutes**
    **Impact: None (caught in CI)**
end note

== Coverage Thresholds ==

note as CoverageNote #FFF5E5
    **Optional: Coverage Requirements**

    ```yaml
    - name: Check coverage threshold
      run: |
        COVERAGE=$(jq '.statistics.registry_coverage' \
                   validation_output/live_check.json)

        # Require 80% registry coverage
        if (( $(echo "$COVERAGE < 0.80" | bc -l) )); then
          echo "❌ Coverage too low: $COVERAGE"
          exit 1
        fi
    ```

    **Use cases:**
    - Ensure critical paths instrumented
    - Prevent coverage regression
    - Guide test improvement
end note

@enduml
